WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.202
-Hello, everyone,
and welcome once again

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:03.369
to "Late Night on Lockdown."

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:06.172
My staff and I are still at home
social distancing

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:08.407
and doing our part
to slow the spread,

00:00:08.407 --> 00:00:10.109
which everyone should be doing.

00:00:10.109 --> 00:00:12.344
On Monday, we did our
"Closer Look" from a hallway.

00:00:12.344 --> 00:00:14.780
But I was asked to move
because hallways are,

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:17.083
by design, thoroughfares.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:18.651
So I might be in
a different location,

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:21.421
but the story
is very much the same --

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:23.456
the rapidly spreading
coronavirus outbreak

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:25.324
and the crisis of leadership
at the federal level.

00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:28.127
And now the president
and some of his allies

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:31.364
are saying we should care more
about the stock market

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:32.632
than saving lives.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:35.502
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:40.106
From the very start
of this crisis,

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:41.641
Donald Trump
has desperately tried

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:43.342
to wish it away
with magical thinking,

00:00:43.342 --> 00:00:45.645
which makes sense
because for most of his life,

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:47.480
magical thinking
has worked for him.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.982
I mean, he's failed at virtually
everything he's ever done,

00:00:49.982 --> 00:00:53.186
but magically he always
avoids consequences,

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:56.922
like in the '80s and '90s when
he lost over a billion dollars

00:00:56.922 --> 00:00:59.325
and he dressed like this.

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:02.094
Takes magical thinking
to think that outfit works.

00:01:02.094 --> 00:01:04.930
He looks like an out-of-work
magician on a job interview.

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:08.701
[ As Donald Trump ] My last gig,
let's just say it...disappeared.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:11.070
[ Normal voice ] Looks like
he got banned from performing

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.540
at kids' birthday parties for
doing cocaine in the bathroom.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.741
[ As Donald Trump ]
[ Sniffs ] Hey, Jimmy.

00:01:15.741 --> 00:01:18.311
How about we put a little icing
on that cake?

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:20.179
[ Normal voice ] Trump is
a quintessential con man,

00:01:20.179 --> 00:01:23.048
which is bad when you're running
a casino into the ground,

00:01:23.048 --> 00:01:25.618
but it's especially bad
when you're in charge

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:27.654
of responding
to a deadly pandemic

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:29.955
ravaging the country's
healthcare system

00:01:29.955 --> 00:01:31.423
and cratering the economy.

00:01:31.423 --> 00:01:33.893
This is a situation
everyone was worried about

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:36.829
when we decided to put the most
self-centered man on earth

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:38.497
in the most powerful office
on earth.

00:01:38.497 --> 00:01:41.233
It's like those stories you hear
about a small town

00:01:41.233 --> 00:01:43.403
that elects a dog
as mayor every year.

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:46.239
Sure, you know, it might seem
fun at the time, dog mayor,

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:48.307
but what happens when
there's a thunderstorm

00:01:48.307 --> 00:01:50.910
and you need the mayor
to coordinate disaster relief

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:54.180
but he won't come out
from underneath the couch?

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.015
Trump's fundamentally unequipped

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:58.717
to handle the reality
of a situation like this

00:01:58.717 --> 00:02:01.120
because he has never dwelled
in reality.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.590
His entire life has been built
on magical thinking,

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:06.358
and that's what we've seen
since the start of this crisis,

00:02:06.358 --> 00:02:09.128
like when he literally
said the problem

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:11.096
would disappear miraculously.

00:02:11.096 --> 00:02:14.166
Even his intelligence reports
and public health experts

00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:17.203
were warning him that it
would be extremely dangerous.

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:18.704
-We're going down, not up.

00:02:18.704 --> 00:02:20.573
We're going very substantially
down, not up.

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:22.508
You know, in theory,
when it gets a little warmer,

00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:25.277
it miraculously goes away --
Hope that's true.

00:02:25.277 --> 00:02:28.514
-The coronavirus is very much
under control in the USA.

00:02:28.514 --> 00:02:30.282
-It will go away.
Just stay calm.

00:02:30.282 --> 00:02:32.818
Be calm.
It's really working out.

00:02:32.818 --> 00:02:35.021
And a lot of good things
are gonna happen.

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:36.889
It's going to disappear one day.

00:02:36.889 --> 00:02:38.891
It's like a miracle.
It will disappear.

00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:41.961
-God, he sounds like he's doing
affirmations in a mirror.

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:43.095
It's like an eighth grader

00:02:43.095 --> 00:02:44.831
trying to get psyched up
for a school dance.

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:47.133
"Yes, you have
a huge zit right now,

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:49.968
but one day it will disappear
like a miracle!"

00:02:49.968 --> 00:02:52.605
Also, the last person any of us
should trust on miracles

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:53.939
is Donald Trump.

00:02:53.939 --> 00:02:57.343
I doubt he could name one
actual miracle from the Bible.

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:59.412
[ As Donald Trump ]
Well, let's see.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:01.547
Everyone knows
Jesus cured a leopard,

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:05.885
got rid of its spots so it could
leave the leopard colony.

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:07.986
[ Normal voice ] Also, the least
effective way to calm someone

00:03:07.986 --> 00:03:09.021
is to say, "Be calm."

00:03:09.021 --> 00:03:10.389
That's how you talk
to a dog in heat.

00:03:10.389 --> 00:03:13.726
"Lucy, be calm.
Stop humping everyone's leg."

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:15.094
You can't just tell someone
to be calm.

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:16.495
You actually have to be calming.

00:03:16.495 --> 00:03:19.365
Doctors calm you down by telling
you how they're gonna treat you.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.534
They don't walk into
your exam room and say,

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:22.902
"Okay, we got your CAT scan.

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:24.870
Be calm."

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:26.940
You see, in his addled
childlike mind,

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.907
Trump thought
that by simply acting

00:03:28.907 --> 00:03:31.477
as if the problem wasn't there,
it would go away,

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:34.847
which I can tell you
from trying...

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:36.582
that doesn't work.

00:03:36.582 --> 00:03:38.751
Of course, Trump's
happy talk didn't work.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:41.087
The virus did not
miraculously disappear.

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:44.490
There are now more than
50,000 cases in the U.S.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:47.092
The World Health Organization
said on Tuesday

00:03:47.092 --> 00:03:49.395
there's been a very large
acceleration

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:52.264
of cases in the U.S.
and that it has the potential

00:03:52.264 --> 00:03:54.867
to become the next epicenter
of the outbreak.

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:57.637
And in New York,
Governor Andrew Cuomo

00:03:57.637 --> 00:04:00.606
said on Tuesday
the spread is accelerating

00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:02.307
faster than anticipated.

00:04:02.307 --> 00:04:04.743
He warned other states
that they're gonna experience

00:04:04.743 --> 00:04:07.180
what New York is dealing with
and put it this way...

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.515
-One of the forecasters
said to me,

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:13.286
"We were looking at a freight
train coming across the country.

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:15.788
We're now looking at
a bullet train,"

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:18.524
because the numbers are going up
that quickly.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:20.093
-That's right, a bullet train.

00:04:20.093 --> 00:04:21.661
And that's scary
because Americans

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:23.328
have never seen
public transportation

00:04:23.328 --> 00:04:24.863
as fast as a bullet train
before.

00:04:24.863 --> 00:04:27.967
Our trains are basically
just public bathrooms on rails.

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:30.236
True story, in New York,
the F train

00:04:30.236 --> 00:04:33.372
is just an old-fashioned handcar
operated by two rats.

00:04:33.372 --> 00:04:35.674
And it's not just Cuomo
sounding the alarm.

00:04:35.674 --> 00:04:38.076
This week began with
the Surgeon General

00:04:38.076 --> 00:04:41.280
issuing a dire message to
Americans on the "Today" show,

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:44.450
warning them that things
are about to get very bad

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:47.052
and pleading with people
to stop showing up

00:04:47.052 --> 00:04:48.387
to large public sites,

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:51.023
like the cherry blossoms
in Washington, D.C.

00:04:51.023 --> 00:04:54.861
-I want America to understand,
this week, it's gonna get bad.

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:58.231
And we really need to come
together as a nation.

00:04:58.231 --> 00:05:01.634
I heard the story
that you were just playing,

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:03.703
young people out on beaches.

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:07.373
We see here in D.C. that
the district set up a cam

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:10.409
for people to watch
the cherry blossoms.

00:05:10.409 --> 00:05:12.878
You look on the cam, you see
more people walking around

00:05:12.878 --> 00:05:14.213
than you see cherry blossoms.

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:16.949
And this is how the spread
is occurring.

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:19.419
-First of all, no one wants
to tune in to a livestream

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:21.353
to see a bunch of people
walking around.

00:05:21.353 --> 00:05:23.423
That's why zoos
have penguin cams,

00:05:23.423 --> 00:05:25.891
not "dude on his couch
eating Fritos" cams.

00:05:25.891 --> 00:05:26.925
"Honey, look.

00:05:26.925 --> 00:05:29.395
Oh, look, he's going
for a second bag.

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:31.864
Oh, so majestic."

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:34.500
I mean, no one wants
to watch some dude

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:37.970
just sit in his house by himself
talking to a webcam.

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:40.506
So there you go.

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:42.174
The head of the Surgeon General
said it himself --

00:05:42.174 --> 00:05:43.476
This week is gonna be bad.

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:44.977
The governor in New York
called it a bullet train,

00:05:44.977 --> 00:05:47.547
and the WHO said the U.S. could
become the next epicenter.

00:05:47.547 --> 00:05:50.115
Or, as the president put it
on Tuesday...

00:05:50.115 --> 00:05:53.285
-Ultimately, the goal
is to ease the guidelines

00:05:53.285 --> 00:05:56.955
and open things up to very large
sections of our country

00:05:56.955 --> 00:05:59.791
as we near the end
of our historic battle

00:05:59.791 --> 00:06:01.494
with the invisible enemy.

00:06:01.494 --> 00:06:03.996
There's tremendous hope
as we look forward

00:06:03.996 --> 00:06:07.166
and we begin to see the light
at the end of the tunnel.

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:08.734
-Light at the end of the tunnel?

00:06:08.734 --> 00:06:10.936
What are you talking about?

00:06:10.936 --> 00:06:14.006
Are you sure you're not just
staring into the sun again?

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:16.375
[ As Donald Trump ]
We can all see the light

00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:18.877
at the end of the tunnel,
burning our retinas,

00:06:18.877 --> 00:06:21.514
scarring our pupils,
leaving us permanently blind.

00:06:21.514 --> 00:06:22.982
And thanks to that blindness,

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:25.885
we no longer have to look at
boring charts -- so boring --

00:06:25.885 --> 00:06:28.320
telling us things are
getting worse every day.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:30.089
Not a flat curve, no.

00:06:30.089 --> 00:06:31.690
[ Normal voice ] Think about
how deranged this is.

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:33.158
Experts are telling us
it could take months.

00:06:33.158 --> 00:06:35.194
New York is the first
major epicenter.

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:37.497
We're still two or three weeks
away from hitting the peak.

00:06:37.497 --> 00:06:40.232
Nurses and doctors on the front
lines are describing chaos

00:06:40.232 --> 00:06:42.968
and comparing ERs to war zones.

00:06:42.968 --> 00:06:45.838
And the president is claiming
it's almost over.

00:06:45.838 --> 00:06:47.806
Finding out what World War II
would've been like

00:06:47.806 --> 00:06:51.410
if FDR had said,
"December 7, 1941,

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:55.581
a date that will live in infamy
as the end of World War II!

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:57.749
Smoke 'em if you got 'em, boys.

00:06:57.749 --> 00:06:59.418
We've wrapped it up."

00:06:59.418 --> 00:07:02.054
Trump has always cared more
about the stock market

00:07:02.054 --> 00:07:03.622
than the public health crisis.

00:07:03.622 --> 00:07:05.791
He cares more about the Dow
than saving lives.

00:07:05.791 --> 00:07:06.858
It's that simple.

00:07:06.858 --> 00:07:08.260
He sees the stock market as key

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:09.961
to his personal
political fortune,

00:07:09.961 --> 00:07:11.130
so now he's talking about

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.998
lifting the public
health restrictions

00:07:12.998 --> 00:07:15.067
and opening the country back up
by Easter --

00:07:15.067 --> 00:07:17.870
Easter, which is less
than three weeks away.

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:20.940
-I'd love to have it open
by Easter, okay?

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:22.708
I would love to have it open
by Easter.

00:07:22.708 --> 00:07:24.543
I will tell you that right now.

00:07:24.543 --> 00:07:26.111
I would love to have that.

00:07:26.111 --> 00:07:28.547
It's such an important day
for other reasons,

00:07:28.547 --> 00:07:31.117
but I'll make it an important
day for this, too.

00:07:31.117 --> 00:07:34.921
I would love to have
the country opened up

00:07:34.921 --> 00:07:37.689
and just raring to go by Easter.

00:07:37.689 --> 00:07:38.758
-Who suggested that day?

00:07:38.758 --> 00:07:40.326
-I just thought it was
a beautiful time,

00:07:40.326 --> 00:07:42.728
a beautiful time,
a beautiful timeline.

00:07:42.728 --> 00:07:44.062
It's a great day.

00:07:44.062 --> 00:07:46.198
-So you just came up
with that yourself?

00:07:46.198 --> 00:07:48.767
You're literally onstage
with multiple doctors,

00:07:48.767 --> 00:07:51.437
and you decided to cede
the decision to this guy?

00:07:51.437 --> 00:07:54.206
[ As Donald Trump ]
He's bringing the eggs
whether we like it or not.

00:07:54.206 --> 00:07:55.707
I say be ready.

00:07:55.707 --> 00:07:57.509
[ Normal voice ] Don't just
pull dates out of your ass.

00:07:57.509 --> 00:07:59.645
For one thing,
that is unsanitary,

00:07:59.645 --> 00:08:02.281
and you should wash your hands
all the time.

00:08:02.281 --> 00:08:05.150
And, two, don't ruin Easter.
You're terrible at Easter.

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:07.486
Every year you give a rambling
speech to the children

00:08:07.486 --> 00:08:09.121
at the White House
Easter Egg Roll

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:11.424
with that shocked Easter Bunny
standing next to you,

00:08:11.424 --> 00:08:14.327
you know, the one that always
looks like he just walked in

00:08:14.327 --> 00:08:16.428
on his wife having sex
with his brother.

00:08:16.428 --> 00:08:20.266
"Deborah, what about
our 30 children?"

00:08:20.266 --> 00:08:22.568
Remember, this is a real thing
the president said

00:08:22.568 --> 00:08:25.037
at the White House Easter Egg
Roll just two years ago.

00:08:25.037 --> 00:08:29.108
-Also, I want to thank the White
House Historical Association

00:08:29.108 --> 00:08:32.845
and all of the people that
worked so hard with Melania,

00:08:32.845 --> 00:08:36.649
with everybody to keep this
incredible house or building

00:08:36.649 --> 00:08:38.784
or whatever you want to call it,

00:08:38.784 --> 00:08:41.587
because there really is no name
for it.

00:08:41.587 --> 00:08:43.189
It is special.

00:08:43.189 --> 00:08:46.659
And we keep it in tip-top shape.

00:08:46.659 --> 00:08:49.495
We call it sometimes
tippy-top shape.

00:08:49.495 --> 00:08:51.897
-Just a reminder,
we have a president

00:08:51.897 --> 00:08:53.833
in charge of a pandemic response

00:08:53.833 --> 00:08:56.502
who couldn't remember
the name White House

00:08:56.502 --> 00:09:00.005
and who sometimes calls "tip-top
shape" "tippy-top shape."

00:09:00.005 --> 00:09:01.406
We're [bleep]

00:09:01.406 --> 00:09:04.943
Or as I sometimes call it
[bleep] [bleep] [bleep]

00:09:04.943 --> 00:09:07.379
Not only did Trump randomly
and arbitrarily

00:09:07.379 --> 00:09:10.349
concoct a date out of nowhere
for reopening the country

00:09:10.349 --> 00:09:13.485
against the advice of virtually
all public health experts,

00:09:13.485 --> 00:09:15.754
he actually suggested
he wanted churches

00:09:15.754 --> 00:09:17.990
to be filled with worshipers
on Easter.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:22.595
Look, Easter's
a very special day for me.

00:09:22.595 --> 00:09:24.563
And I see it sort of
in that timeline

00:09:24.563 --> 00:09:25.831
that I'm thinking about.

00:09:25.831 --> 00:09:27.499
And I say, "Wouldn't it be great

00:09:27.499 --> 00:09:29.401
to have all of
the churches full"?

00:09:29.401 --> 00:09:32.104
You know, the churches
aren't allowed, essentially,

00:09:32.104 --> 00:09:34.139
to have much
of a congregation there.

00:09:34.139 --> 00:09:35.875
So I think Easter Sunday,

00:09:35.875 --> 00:09:39.478
and you'll have packed churches
all over our country.

00:09:39.478 --> 00:09:41.914
I think it would be
a beautiful time.

00:09:41.914 --> 00:09:44.750
-Wait. So your plan to deal with
a very contagious disease

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:47.720
is to pack as many people as
possible into enclosed spaces,

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:51.456
have them touch their faces,
and drink out of the same cup?

00:09:51.456 --> 00:09:52.891
I mean, let's face it.

00:09:52.891 --> 00:09:56.362
That's not even a great idea
when there isn't a pandemic.

00:09:56.362 --> 00:09:58.063
It's almost like he's trying

00:09:58.063 --> 00:10:00.900
to get as many people sick
as he possibly can.

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:04.069
I mean, remember when he
announced his poorly planned

00:10:04.069 --> 00:10:05.537
and confusing travel ban

00:10:05.537 --> 00:10:08.607
and throngs of people
rushing back into the country

00:10:08.607 --> 00:10:11.577
packed into airports
and waited online for hours?

00:10:11.577 --> 00:10:13.145
What's Trump gonna do next,

00:10:13.145 --> 00:10:16.015
hold a giant music festival
called "Cough-chella"?

00:10:16.015 --> 00:10:17.116
[ As Donald Trump ]
Bad news, guys.

00:10:17.116 --> 00:10:18.750
It's just the one porta-potty.

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:20.352
Bad planning.
That's on me.

00:10:20.352 --> 00:10:22.421
[ Normal voice ] Obviously
public health experts

00:10:22.421 --> 00:10:24.556
are aghast at this idea.

00:10:24.556 --> 00:10:25.991
Last week, one of the world's

00:10:25.991 --> 00:10:28.628
leading infectious disease
experts, Dr. Anthony Fauci,

00:10:28.628 --> 00:10:30.662
known for facepalming
in the background

00:10:30.662 --> 00:10:31.864
as the president speaks,

00:10:31.864 --> 00:10:33.699
dismissed it as crazy
and heartless

00:10:33.699 --> 00:10:35.267
at a White House press briefing.

00:10:35.267 --> 00:10:37.269
